Line 2: An email address goes in quotes, like "team@ourcompany.com".
    email the list to team@ourcompany.com.
                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
EasyScript can't send email yet, but it can keep an address as text.

Line 5: EasyScript can't use the internet yet.
    look up the status at https://track.example.com/?id=5.
                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
It can read files on this computer, like "read the table in "data.csv" and call it data".

Line 1: EasyScript can't send email yet.
    send the report to "team@shop.com".
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
It can write the text into a file for you to send, like "write report in file "report.txt"".

Line 3: EasyScript can't send email yet.
    every monday at 9am email "bookings.csv" to "team@ourcompany.com"
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
It can write the text into a file for you to send, like "write report in file "report.txt"".

Line 4: EasyScript can't make web pages yet.
    make a web page where guests can sign up.
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
It can ask questions in the terminal, like "ask "What's your name?" and call it name".

Line 6: EasyScript can't use the internet yet.
    get the page at "https://example.com".
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
It can read files on this computer, like "read the table in "data.csv" and call it data".

Line 7: EasyScript can't read Excel files yet.
    read the table in "listings.xlsx" and call it listings.
    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Save the sheet as a csv file in Excel ("Save As", then "CSV"), and read that.
